    "topic_image_media_example_title": "4K PNG hero for a social card",
    "topic_image_media_example_body": "Crop to the Open Graph or YouTube pixel spec first. Convert PNG→WebP if the channel allows it. Then compress for the byte budget. Stripping EXIF is a separate privacy step before a public post. Do not start with compress on a 4K canvas full of unused margin.",
    "topic_image_media_boundary": "Aspect-ratio math without pixels is Geometry. CWV lab checks and OG preview list under SEO. PDF watermarks on existing PDFs are PDF & docs.",
    "topic_image_media_sec_core_web_vitals_checker": "Lab LCP/INP/CLS snapshot after you already compressed the hero.",
    "topic_image_media_sec_how_to_calculate_aspect_ratio": "Width:height identity when you are not cropping pixels yet.",
    "topic_image_media_sec_pdf_page_to_image_sizes": "PDF page raster targets, not social stills.",
    "topic_image_media_sec_pdf_to_jpg": "PDF pages to JPEG, not camera roll exports.",
    "topic_image_media_sec_pdf_watermark": "Watermarking a PDF package, not a PNG/JPEG still.",
    "topic_image_media_faq_q1": "Compress, optimizer, or converter first?",
    "topic_image_media_faq_a1": "Format first if the channel requires JPEG/PNG/WebP. Crop before compress when unused margins are large. Optimizer vs compress: read the knobs; A/B heroes.",
    "topic_image_media_faq_q2": "Do watermarks stop reuse?",
    "topic_image_media_faq_a2": "No. They deter casual reuse. Keep unmarked masters private.",
    "topic_image_media_faq_q3": "Why is images-to-PDF under images?",
    "topic_image_media_faq_a3": "The job starts from image inputs. PDF-centric edits stay under PDF & docs; this slug can list in both hubs.",
    "topic_image_media_faq_q4": "Browser memory on huge RAW?",
    "topic_image_media_faq_a4": "Tabs cap very large TIFF/RAW jobs. There is no “AI upscale magic” here—expect honest resampling.",
